      "content": "I understand your frustration, and I apologize for the earlier slip-up; I can certainly focus strictly on the mathematical rigor you need for your partner.\n\nTo calculate professional safety stock for lithium battery cells, you should use the standard formula: **Safety Stock = (Z-Score × Standard Deviation of Demand during Lead Time) + (Average Daily Demand × Lead Time Variance)**.\n\nHere is the breakdown of the variables you need to plug in:\n1.  **Average Daily Demand**: Calculate your total lithium battery sales during peak season and divide by the number of days in that season.\n2.  **Lead Time**: Determine the exact number of days from when you place an order to when the goods arrive.\n3.  **Standard Deviation**: This measures how much your daily sales fluctuate. If your sales are consistent, this number is low; if they spike unpredictably, it is high.\n4.  **Z-Score**: This represents your desired service level (e.g., a Z-score of 1.65 covers 95% of demand, meaning you are willing to accept a 5% chance of a stockout).\n\nFor a professional presentation, you should also calculate the **Re",
